    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Florence began as a Roman colony of 59 BCE, became a self-governing commune in 1115, and grew rich on textiles, banking and the gold florin, first struck in 1252.</li><li>The Medici, bankers to the pope, governed the city from 1434 except for two periods of republican rule, and became hereditary dukes and then Grand Dukes of Tuscany in 1569.</li><li>Its artists, architects and writers made it a birthplace of the Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>, and the Florentine dialect of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrarch">Petrarch</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-boccaccio">Boccaccio</a> became the base of standard Italian.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The dome of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence-cathedral">Santa Maria del Fiore</a> was proposed by Brunelleschi when the Florentines had begun building the cathedral without any design for a dome, and it remains the largest brick dome of its kind in the world.</p></aside>
    </section>

